tnt-chat (1.3.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Make the non-modal keymap the default; reach vim with /vim or vim@host.
  * Compose multi-line messages with Ctrl-J and Alt-Enter.
  * Render text at its true width and wrap long messages instead of truncating.
  * Edit the message line at the caret with the arrow, Home, End, and Delete keys.
  * Render a markdown subset: bold, inline code, fenced blocks, and bare URLs.
  * Escape message log content and migrate existing logs on first start.
  * Make the module response deadline configurable and let modules send newlines.

 -- M1ng <contact@m1ng.space>  Wed, 16 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0800

tnt-chat (1.3.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Replace the Markdown documentation set with installed manual pages.
  * Bound incomplete SSH logins so stalled setups release their slots.
  * Isolate TUI tokenizer state and drop cron maintenance privileges.
  * Detach tntctl stdin so a remote command cannot drain caller input.
  * Harden module, input, and release gates for constrained hosts.

